# FIXTURE — the generated CPF as the flow writes it today: VDD and VSS only.
# The io-rail-ir-drop gap's refuted_by must exit 1 over this file (gap still
# real). Modelled on the shape of the real 21-line *_gate1.cpf (set_cpf_version
# / set_design / create_power_domain / create_ground_nets / create_power_nets);
# the values are synthetic.
#
# THE PREREQUISITE IS NOT A TOOL, IT IS THE POWER INTENT. Because this file
# declares no VDDIO/VSSIO, report_power cannot attribute the IO group to them
# and files ~30% of chip power on an unnamed Default rail at the CORE voltage.
# Adding those nets to a rail run WITHOUT routing to analyse would return ~0 mV
# and look excellent — a false green by construction, which is why the ir-drop
# stage excludes the IO ring BY NAME.
#
# TWO DECOYS, both near-misses of '^create_power_nets .*VDDIO':
#   * a COMMENTED create_power_nets line naming VDDIO. The regex anchors at
#     column 1, so a `#` must defeat it — this is how a proposal in a comment
#     gets read as power intent.
#   * an INDENTED create_power_nets line naming VDDIO, in the dead
#     hand-written-CPF branch. Same anchor, and this one is the live hazard:
#     the hand-written nanosoc_chip_pads.cpf does declare the IO rails, and the
#     gap is about the CPF THE FLOW ACTUALLY READS.
#
# TWO `.__exclusive__` MARKERS, AND WHAT THEY DO. The probe GLOBS
# (`ASIC/eth-chiplet/build/*/outputs/*_gate1.cpf`), and globbing follows the
# symlinks a sandbox is built from. Without the marker on
# ASIC/eth-chiplet/build/ the sandbox sees SIX real generated CPFs — including
# the one belonging to whatever P&R run is in flight — and the case is decided
# by a seven-file grep instead of by this fixture.
#
# MEASURED, and stated because it is less than it looks: none of those six
# declares VDDIO at column 1 today, so both halves would reach the same verdict
# with the markers removed. The markers buy ISOLATION, not the verdict — the
# refuted half would otherwise be passing on a grep across seven files, six of
# them live build output that changes under it. A proof whose inputs move is not
# a proof, and this is the same reason `drc` carries one.
set_cpf_version 2.0

set_design nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads

create_power_domain -name PD_TOP \
    -default

create_ground_nets -nets VSS
create_power_nets -nets VDD

# create_power_nets -nets VDDIO -voltage 3.3   ;# NOT DECLARED. See gap io-rail-ir-drop.
# create_ground_nets -nets VSSIO               ;# NOT DECLARED.

# from the dead hand-written intent, never read by the flow:
  create_power_nets -nets VDDIO -voltage 3.3
  create_ground_nets -nets VSSIO

end_design
